{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window","id":1088689,"title":"Can others see your scrying window?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-06T03:50:08-07:00","id":1088689,"title":"Can others see your scrying window?","content":"Hi everyone, sorry if this was asked before or of the answer is extremely obvious.<br /> <br /> If a mage casts Scry, how does their end of the scrying window manifest? I have a Mastigos with a &quot;scrying room&quot; who projects his scrying windows on various mirrors there.<br /> <br /> What I'm curious about is can other mages see those images? Can sleepers? Can it be recorded using mundane means?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13239-ashenknight","name":"AshenKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:08:48-07:00","id":1088692,"title":"","content":"I thought there was a Reach effect to explicitly make the windows one-way? I might be mis-rememebering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:26:00-07:00","id":1088696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088692#post1088692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there was a Reach effect to explicitly make the windows one-way? I might be mis-rememebering.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for the subject's end, not the mage's, and there's no Reach required.<br /> <br /> Since adding Fate 2 allows the mage to make the window selectively perceptible from the other end, replicating that effect on the mage's end would be reasonable.<br /> <br /> Scrying doesn't need to be cast on mirrors, so I guess the scrying room is just the warlock's Yantra of choice or his Sanctum?<br /> <br /> Everyone, mage or not, should be able to see the caster's end of the Scrying window, unless you allow Fate 2 to selectively disallow it like I said. Allowing a Sleeper to do so, however, will quickly trigger Dissonance and Quiescence. The window could be recorded, I guess, but I don't quite remember the rules on recorded magical phenomena. Knee-jerk reaction is to say that Dissonance mucks up the recording and Quiescence makes everyone forget about it, but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T04:47:32-07:00","id":1088701,"title":"","content":"Fate 2 component is bullshit. Just use Key mechanics that are part of the Space Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:01:42-07:00","id":1088706,"title":"","content":"It triggers Peripheral Mage Sight, and is clearly visible in Space Active Mage Sight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T05:49:28-07:00","id":1088716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088706#post1088706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It triggers Peripheral Mage Sight, and is clearly visible in Space Active Mage Sight</div> </div> </div> </div>Only visible with active space sight, or is it not clearly visible but still visible without it? Does this mean the mage using it needs active space sight up to use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:06:07-07:00","id":1088736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088701#post1088701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate 2 component is bullshit. Just use Key mechanics that are part of the Space Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bullshit, it allows for -selective- two way viewing. In other words, normally, you can make the window one way, or two way, but with Fate you can make it two way for you and your friend you're scrying on, but even though he's in a crowd no one else can see it because for them it's one way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:30:38-07:00","id":1088748,"title":"","content":"You could also Key it with 'Be You Or Your Friend' to perceive the window. Quite selective without the need of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:36:12-07:00","id":1088751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088696#post1088696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's for the subject's end, not the mage's, and there's no Reach required.<br /> <br /> Since adding Fate 2 allows the mage to make the window selectively perceptible from the other end, replicating that effect on the mage's end would be reasonable.<br /> <br /> Scrying doesn't need to be cast on mirrors, so I guess the scrying room is just the warlock's Yantra of choice or his Sanctum?<br /> <br /> Everyone, mage or not, should be able to see the caster's end of the Scrying window, unless you allow Fate 2 to selectively disallow it like I said. Allowing a Sleeper to do so, however, will quickly trigger Dissonance and Quiescence. The window could be recorded, I guess, but I don't quite remember the rules on recorded magical phenomena. Knee-jerk reaction is to say that Dissonance mucks up the recording and Quiescence makes everyone forget about it, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks a bunch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I thought so, but I wanted to run it by the knowledgeable people here. <br /> <br /> And yes, the mirror room is a yantra, I just liked the image of a warlock having multiple scrying windows open and monitoring his targets. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13239-ashenknight","name":"AshenKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:40:09-07:00","id":1088753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088706#post1088706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It triggers Peripheral Mage Sight, and is clearly visible in Space Active Mage Sight</div> </div> </div> </div>This means on the subject end correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:48:29-07:00","id":1088756,"title":"","content":"If only active space sight makes it visible then you dont need to worry about sleepers seeing it.<br /> <br /> Im hoping Dave just meant that normally everybody can see the window at the targets end (unless made selective) but if its one way or selective then active space sight will still notice it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:52:46-07:00","id":1088757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088756#post1088756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only active space sight makes it visible then you dont need to worry about sleepers seeing it.<br /> <br /> Im hoping Dave just meant that normally everybody can see the window at the targets end (unless made selective) but if its one way or selective then active space sight will still notice it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the second option was his intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:08:45-07:00","id":1088773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088748#post1088748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also Key it with 'Be You Or Your Friend' to perceive the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the narrative function of Keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:42:10-07:00","id":1088781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088773#post1088773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the narrative function of Keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the narrative function of Keys then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:46:57-07:00","id":1088782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088781#post1088781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the narrative function of Keys then?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you start allowing +1 reach to give spells a key that says &quot;my friends&quot; to avoid needing fate, then fraying aoe damage spells become OP. Dont get me wrong, ive seen from alot of your replies that you allow alot of things i personally wouldnt allow in my games and thats fine but by RAW, scrying has no key option so this will have to come down to creative thaum territory and each ST playing and allowing different things in their own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T09:52:47-07:00","id":1088783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088748#post1088748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also Key it with 'Be You Or Your Friend' to perceive the window. Quite selective without the need of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, How does the spell know who your friends are? What if you decide midway through a spells duration that a person isnt your friend anymore? No i think Keys need to have abit of solid criteria to them. There must be something for a key to detect thats not based on how you feel at a particular time?<br /> <br /> Red heads, My bloodline, anybody holding X. I think &quot;My friends&quot; falls into fate territory and isnt concrete enough as a key?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T10:11:11-07:00","id":1088790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088782#post1088782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you start allowing +1 reach to give spells a key that says &quot;my friends&quot; to avoid needing fate, then fraying aoe damage spells become OP. Dont get me wrong, ive seen from alot of your replies that you allow alot of things i personally wouldnt allow in my games and thats fine but by RAW, scrying has no key option so this will have to come down to creative thaum territory and each ST playing and allowing different things in their own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea. Sure there is that clause with 'here is the Key mechanic but use it only with spells we specifically pointed. since we have no word count for rules which spells in c.thaum can be Keyed you cant do it', I know, I know. So like always this is my homebrew take on it: I allow every arcanum to have it's key based on purview, Fate and Space are just darn best for it. With Death you could key something to be used only by injured or dying individuals, with Life you could specify a gender, hair color, Prime - mage, Mind - someone calm, etc. Things that you could generally perceive with a specific AMS.<br /> <br /> Back to Fate. If you can cast 'OP' aoe damage spells with Fate why Space can't do it too?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088783#post1088783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, How does the spell know who your friends are? What if you decide midway through a spells duration that a person isnt your friend anymore? No i think Keys need to have abit of solid criteria to them. There must be something for a key to detect thats not based on how you feel at a particular time?<br /> <br /> Red heads, My bloodline, anybody holding X. I think &quot;My friends&quot; falls into fate territory and isnt concrete enough as a key?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right and I wasn't precise enough - I meant <i>This</i> Particular Friend - points finger. You could also key it for Only Strong Sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T18:15:21-07:00","id":1088929,"title":"","content":"Space spells don't require the spell itself to be explicit about whether or not it can have a key. That's not how keys work. Rather, a key is something that unlocks/locks the space because you can lock/unlock doors and windows and other liminal spaces. Space magic is reflecting from the phenomenal into the supernal (or vice versa if you think that people's ideas of locks and keys on windows and doors comes from the supernal). In that aspect locking a scrying window so that it is visible to only certain people on your end makes sense. The fate inclusion is for the other end of the window.<br /> <br /> By this same token, keys are not an all arcana thing. You can't lock up the electricity in an area for only those that are red heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T18:52:39-07:00","id":1088944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088929#post1088929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By this same token, keys are not an all arcana thing. You can't lock up the electricity in an area for only those that are red heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I know that is the case, the mental image alone is amusing enough that I'm now trying to find a way to legitimately do something like this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:35:47-07:00","id":1088985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088781#post1088781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the narrative function of Keys then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding security to a spell's effects that gets more particular the more powerful that spell is, hence why higher Potency lets you add more criteria to the Key and the most personal the examples get is sharing a character's bloodline.<br /> <br /> It's yet another mechanical widget that works to incentivize mages to maintain idiosyncratic behaviors like keeping a wax apple on their person and always wearing at least one article of green clothing. If there's no conceivable way for a Key to be used through guile or accident, it's not doing the job of being part and parcel of Cryptic Wizard Bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T02:06:30-07:00","id":1089045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088929#post1088929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Space spells don't require the spell itself to be explicit about whether or not it can have a key.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spells that can be Keyed are called out below, usually at the<br /> cost of a Reach. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not how keys work. Rather, a key is something that unlocks/locks the space because you can lock/unlock doors and windows and other liminal spaces. Space magic is reflecting from the phenomenal into the supernal (or vice versa if you think that people's ideas of locks and keys on windows and doors comes from the supernal). In that aspect locking a scrying window so that it is visible to only certain people on your end makes sense. The fate inclusion is for the other end of the window. </div> </div> </div>I like this explanation but Fate component for other side of the spell still has no sense. Furthermore, the book isn't consistent with this interpretation. You can't Key a Ban...aand.. yes, I've checked all spells that lock something and it seems pretty consistent. Ban must be an overlook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By this same token, keys are not an all arcana thing. You can't lock up the electricity in an area for only those that are red heads. </div> </div> </div>By RAW you can. With adding Fate 2 or Keying a Ban(if its an overlook).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088985#post1088985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding security to a spell's effects that gets more particular the more powerful that spell is, hence why higher Potency lets you add more criteria to the Key and the most personal the examples get is sharing a character's bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It lets you add more complicated Keys by combining them. One Key per potency. Example potency 3: male, under 1.65m, redhead. If it can check whether somebody is of your bloodline (with single Key) it shouldn't have a problem with 'being a friend'. Spell checks both ways, he can not perceive you as your friend but if you do he is accepted. Other way around he would still be accepted since spell doesn't take sides. If you point a finger at someone and say 'be him' it should be a valid Key, he becomes a password that can be forged with Life 4 or perhaps some clever Veiling<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's yet another mechanical widget that works to incentivize mages to maintain idiosyncratic behaviors like keeping a wax apple on their person and always wearing at least one article of green clothing. If there's no conceivable way for a Key to be used through guile or accident, it's not doing the job of being part and parcel of Cryptic Wizard Bullshit. </div> </div> </div>Well said.<br /> <br /> So here's how I actually use 'Keys' in other arcana. I said Keys but I don't think that it should be called that.<br /> <br /> Lets say you want to Life Veil yourself from coyotes, right? You can. Single simple spell. And its RAW.<br /> Now. Lets say you want to hide yourself from only female coyotes. Why not? Hows it different for Life? You can.<br /> Step it up a bit. You want to look like Mick Jagger, but only to redhead human females under 30(biological age, so there might be something different on an ID). Why not? You can. 'Key' the spell.<br /> <br /> Edit: Heh. Sorry for derailing again. I have a really bad habit of doing that. I just hope it's still somewhat in the spirit of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-07-2017, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:07:06-07:00","id":1089051,"title":"","content":"If you look to what spells have an option to be &quot;Keyed&quot; you'd see that all of them are about passageways, Irises, or closed spaces. It even says in the description about Keys that they're useable on several Space spells because Space is about &quot;portals, doors and similar liminal spaces&quot;. That's why Veil Life isn't intended to be &quot;Keyable&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-07-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:22:04-07:00","id":1089055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089051#post1089051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look to what spells have an option to be &quot;Keyed&quot; you'd see that all of them are about passageways, Irises, or closed spaces. It even says in the description about Keys that they're useable on several Space spells because Space is about &quot;portals, doors and similar liminal spaces&quot;. That's why Veil Life isn't intended to be &quot;Keyable&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Life mage can't hide from people only? He has to hide from all instances of life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:45:35-07:00","id":1089061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089055#post1089055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Life mage can't hide from people only? He has to hide from all instances of life?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point. The point is that &quot;keys&quot; that allow you to bypass the effects of a spell are specific to Space. They're about defined areas and the barriers in between them. That's the purview of Space. If you want to give some kind of specificity to a spell (like targeting a part of a person instead of the person as a whole as an example), add a reach to the spell. Or add Fate 2. Depends on what exactly it is that you're trying to do. But a key to bypass a spell's effects is a Space thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:49:43-07:00","id":1089062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1088773#post1088773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the narrative function of Keys.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of keys specifically mentions &quot;a hidden path might be visible to anyone of the mage\u2019s bloodline&quot; as a valid key. I'm finding it hard to imagine that keying people is somehow invalid, given that statement. Of course, you couldn't just say &quot;my friends&quot;. You would have to list them, or specify some objective feature they have in common.<br /> <br /> Personally I would say that Keying a portal to a person makes it so that the person's presence near the portal opens the portal for others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089045#post1089045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this explanation but Fate component for other side of the spell still has no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fate component allows you to make something visible to only a certain person, without needing a combined veiling spell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089045#post1089045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it can check whether somebody is of your bloodline (with single Key) it shouldn't have a problem with 'being a friend'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it should have a problem with &quot;being a friend&quot;. Your bloodline is an objective fact. Who your friends are is not an objective fact, and should not be a valid key, unless you instead specifically list who your friends are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spell checks both ways, he can not perceive you as your friend but if you do he is accepted. Other way around he would still be accepted since spell doesn't take sides. </div> </div> </div>Even your own perception of who your friends are is not an objective fact, even assuming that the spell can read your mind. If your friend has been engaging in suspicious behavior, causing you to doubt them, do they stop being your friend due to your doubts? If you can't clearly and specifically define &quot;friend&quot;, then you can't create the necessary imago to cast the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-07-2017, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T03:52:21-07:00","id":1089063,"title":"","content":"The Life mage can't use Keys to hide from specific instances of life because that's not what Keys are for. You'd have better luck incorporating some Fate since Fate has at least one spell and a few conjunctional effects for selectively ignoring subjects. Or casting a spell on the specific animals that makes them unable to see you rather than making you invisible to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:02:01-07:00","id":1089065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089061#post1089061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the point. The point is that &quot;keys&quot; that allow you to bypass the effects of a spell are specific to Space. They're about defined areas and the barriers in between them. That's the purview of Space. If you want to give some kind of specificity to a spell (like targeting a part of a person instead of the person as a whole as an example), add a reach to the spell. Or add Fate 2. Depends on what exactly it is that you're trying to do. But a key to bypass a spell's effects is a Space thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Key is just a name of reach effect. Its on to something but not really there. It works for Space by 'unlocking' spells with quite abstract Keys that are really not part of Space purview, and its unique here, and for Fate. Other arcana can't get to this level of abstract but certainly can limit scope of casted spell to specified part of their purview. I still call it 'Keys' but something like 'Shutters' might be more suitable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089063#post1089063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Life mage can't use Keys to hide from specific instances of life because that's not what Keys are for. You'd have better luck incorporating some Fate since Fate has at least one spell and a few conjunctional effects for selectively ignoring subjects. Or casting a spell on the specific animals that makes them unable to see you rather than making you invisible to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate has enough privileges as it is now. By 'Key' I mean limiting scope of the spell. Like Death mage who can hide itself from ghosts or vampires or both at the same time.<br /> <br /> 'Shutter' is a good word. I'll use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T04:13:04-07:00","id":1089069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089062#post1089062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of keys specifically mentions &quot;a hidden path might be visible to anyone of the mage\u2019s bloodline&quot; as a valid key. I'm finding it hard to imagine that keying people is somehow invalid, given that statement. Of course, you couldn't just say &quot;my friends&quot;. You would have to list them, or specify some objective feature they have in common.<br /> <br /> Personally I would say that Keying a portal to a person makes it so that the person's presence near the portal opens the portal for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Visible to anyone of the mage's bloodline indicates that it is visible only to the Key or someone with the Key. If you 'posses' mages son, cuffed or something, you can open it, perhaps. This example is a case of 'have this qualities to see' and if you don't have them you cant see. If caster specified that you need 'mages bloodline' instead of 'be of mages bloodline' you just need this Key. Kidnap or ask it to come with you. It'll open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:19:28-07:00","id":1089126,"title":"","content":"Colocates key effect also mentions the key allowing use, so while the default key description says it can activate the spell, if you have keyed it to a bloodline, then only those of the bloodline can activate &amp; use the portal.<br /> <br /> The hidden path is visible to the bloodline because keys can be setup to bypass spells too, so whoever has/is the key bypasses the veiling spell. If you kidnap one of the bloodline they would bypass the spell, but you would still be under its effect and would have to bypass it some other way.<br /> <br /> Call whatever your doing whatever you like but you really shouldnt be spreading your personal view as if it was correct. It isnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T07:28:04-07:00","id":1089132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089126#post1089126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Colocates key effect also mentions the key allowing use, so while the default key description says it can activate the spell, if you have keyed it to a bloodline, then only those of the bloodline can activate &amp; use the portal.<br /> <br /> The hidden path is visible to the bloodline because keys can be setup to bypass spells too, so whoever has/is the key bypasses the veiling spell. If you kidnap one of the bloodline they would bypass the spell, but you would still be under its effect and would have to bypass it some other way.<br /> <br /> Call whatever your doing whatever you like but you really shouldnt be spreading your personal view as if it was correct. It isnt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry but where this is different from my last post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:50:19-07:00","id":1089355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089069#post1089069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Visible to anyone of the mage's bloodline indicates that it is visible only to the Key or someone with the Key. If you 'posses' mages son, cuffed or something, you can open it, perhaps. This example is a case of 'have this qualities to see' and if you don't have them you cant see. If caster specified that you need 'mages bloodline' instead of 'be of mages bloodline' you just need this Key. Kidnap or ask it to come with you. It'll open.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it's a veiling spell, and hiding things is what it does, so selectively hiddng things is what a key does to it. By contrast, if you put a key on a portal or a scrying window, you would not be able to selectively hide things because hiding things is not what those spells do. You could selectively activate the portal, or selectively open the scrying window, but not make it inexplicably visible to one person, even though other people are around.<br /> <br /> As I said, you need Fate to selectively hide things from certain people without a veiling spell, so doing that on a scrying window or a portal would not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-07-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:54:53-07:00","id":1089361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089355#post1089355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because it's a veiling spell. As I said, you need Fate to selectively hide things from certain people without a veiling spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Lure and Repel (Life 2, Ruling) can specify targets just fine. It's not Veiling though, but it's nice example of a spell being build around concept of 'Shutter'*.<br /> And actually, umm, I never said that you can hide things with something different than Veiling.<br /> <br /> *made up by me. homebrew. but rooted in inner workings of spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-07-2017, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:19:08-07:00","id":1089375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089361#post1089361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Lure and Repel (Life 2, Ruling) can specify targets just fine. It's not Veiling though, but it's nice example of a spell being build around concept of 'Shutter'*.<br /> And actually, umm, I never said that you can hide things with something different than Veiling.<br /> <br /> *made up by me. homebrew. but rooted in inner workings of spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does Lure and Repel have to do with selectively hiding things from certain people without a veiling spell?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:31:37-07:00","id":1089385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089355#post1089355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or selectively open the scrying window, but not make it inexplicably visible to one person...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it the same?<br /> <br /> Ok. I'll leave the Shutters and Lure and Repel for now. So 'Keys' are unique Space mechanics to unlock spells that lock, restrict, connect or obscure something. Co-location is not Veiling spell but its effects can be restricted and can be unlocked by a Key. The same goes for Scry - effect can be restricted by raw so you should be able to unlock it with a Key. No visible window=no access. Key=access.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:41:30-07:00","id":1089389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089385#post1089385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Secret Door can make a door that only one person can see. In a room full of people, only the person with the key can notice the passage. Scrying can make a scrying window that opens when certain conditions are met. In a room full of people, if someone satisfies the key, the window becomes visible to EVERYONE. To make it so only the keyholder can see the scrying window, you must use Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T15:48:12-07:00","id":1089434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089045#post1089045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lets you add more complicated Keys by combining them. One Key per potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Key may have a number of requirements equal to the spell's Potency&quot; is not &quot;the spell has a number of Keys equal to its Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it can check whether somebody is of your bloodline (with single Key) it shouldn't have a problem with 'being a friend'. </div> </div> </div>Your bloodline is a static quality that still facilitates weird workarounds like mage ancestors you never knew about or interloping descendants from the future. Friendship does not provide these workarounds and further gets into quibbling minutia like whether someone who plans to betray you counts as a friend. The primary point of Keys is to help lock off effects with use/override requirements, not to act as low-budget mind-reading and simple-intent-based perfect security.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you point a finger at someone and say 'be him' it should be a valid Key </div> </div> </div>It absolutely should not, not least because Buddy Steve is not a quality that gives a mage any reason to bother with other Keys for a closed effect meant to be used by Buddy Steve alone unless they plan on later duplicity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089062#post1089062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of keys specifically mentions &quot;a hidden path might be visible to anyone of the mage\u2019s bloodline&quot; as a valid key. I'm finding it hard to imagine that keying people is somehow invalid, given that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keying <i>specific people</i> by the quality of <i>being those specific people</i>, however, is against the spirit of what Key represent, which is the same sort of peculiar rituals and qualities that characterize the obscure/longform means of opening supernatural gateways in other games; you could make a Pocket Dimension that's only accessible by Disciples of the cabal's highest shared Arcanum who're wearing the cabal's signature colors, carrying an emblem of the cabal's shared symbol, and have been subject to a rote designed by the keeper of the realm within the last decade, but you couldn't just say &quot;Anyone except Arbitrax, Deandr\u00e9, and Thanador is unable to use this door without using magic to jimmy it open.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:43:30-07:00","id":1089466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089434#post1089434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Key may have a number of requirements equal to the spell's Potency&quot; is not &quot;the spell has a number of Keys equal to its Potency.&quot;<br /> <br /> Keying <i>specific people</i> by the quality of <i>being those specific people</i>, however, is against the spirit of what Key represent, which is the same sort of peculiar rituals and qualities that characterize the obscure/longform means of opening supernatural gateways in other games; you could make a Pocket Dimension that's only accessible by Disciples of the cabal's highest shared Arcanum who're wearing the cabal's signature colors, carrying an emblem of the cabal's shared symbol, and have been subject to a rote designed by the keeper of the realm within the last decade, but you couldn't just say &quot;Anyone except Arbitrax, Deandr\u00e9, and Thanador is unable to use this door without using magic to jimmy it open.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Id say keying something by the quality of them being a specific person is fine, since it cant be changed later and is a absolute fact. Keying to &quot;my friend Bob&quot; then suddenly bob isnt your friend to stop Bob using the key however wouldnt work.<br /> <br /> Even a key like &quot;my cabal mates&quot; is a nono. How does the spell know a person is or isnt your cabal mate? You could key it to: Everybody here with me now, him, him, him and her, and then only those people are they keys.<br /> <br /> Your example the keys are &quot;wearing cabals signature colors&quot;, &quot;carrying an emblem&quot; (any emblem of the cabals shared symbol or only those emblemes selected at the time of the spell casting, one could define it as only those emblems present when the spell was cast), &quot;subject to a rote&quot; (not sure on this one, how does the spell know the person had a rote cast on them?). Two of those examples are fine as keys yes, the third is ropey.<br /> <br /> If you can key something to &quot;one of my relations&quot; (then the spell has some way of checking its a relation of you) you can easily key it to &quot;Bob&quot;, the spell will check if its the Bob you keyed and activate/bypass him etc etc.<br /> <br /> If i picked up a peeble and made the key &quot;Anybody holding this peeble.&quot; its a specific key thats keyed to the quality of that peeble. Anybody else holding another peeble isnt going to be the key. Same with specific people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T16:54:20-07:00","id":1089470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089466#post1089466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even a key like &quot;my cabal mates&quot; is a nono. How does the spell know a person is or isnt your cabal mate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being part of a cabal of mages is a thing that tends to pick up symbolism as a function of praxis. Cabal Theme is a Merit that specifically represents a quality that links every member of a given cabal, which gives hooks to hang the Key off of that are less individually particular than &quot;they're in my cabal.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your example the keys are &quot;wearing cabals signature colors&quot;, &quot;carrying an emblem&quot; (any emblem of the cabals shared symbol or only those emblemes selected at the time of the spell casting, one could define it as only those emblems present when the spell was cast), &quot;subject to a rote&quot; (not sure on this one, how does the spell know the person had a rote cast on them?). Two of those examples are fine as keys yes, the third is ropey. </div> </div> </div>I gave genericized examples that would be specific in the context of actual use. (The spell &quot;knows&quot; that the person had a rote cast on them the same way an Avernian Gate knows if you committed a murder in the last day. Mystic history leaves marks.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you can key something to &quot;one of my relations&quot; (then the spell has some way of checking its a relation of you) you can easily key it to &quot;Bob&quot;, the spell will check if its the Bob you keyed and activate/bypass him etc etc.<br /> <br /> If i picked up a peeble and made the key &quot;Anybody holding this peeble.&quot; its a specific key thats keyed to the quality of that peeble. Anybody else holding another peeble isnt going to be the key. Same with specific people. </div> </div> </div>Awakened magic operates on symbolism. Absent famous and/or magical resources, most specific individual entities are not symbols unto themselves; if you want to limit the exploitation of a long-lasting effect to a specific person, you make a Key that narrows the field as closely to that person and that person alone as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T17:17:13-07:00","id":1089478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089470#post1089470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being part of a cabal of mages is a thing that tends to pick up symbolism as a function of praxis. Cabal Theme is a Merit that specifically represents a quality that links every member of a given cabal, which gives hooks to hang the Key off of that are less individually particular than &quot;they're in my cabal.&quot;<br /> <br /> I gave genericized examples that would be specific in the context of actual use. (The spell &quot;knows&quot; that the person had a rote cast on them the same way an Avernian Gate knows if you committed a murder in the last day. Mystic history leaves marks.)<br /> <br /> Awakened magic operates on symbolism. Absent famous and/or magical resources, most specific individual entities are not symbols unto themselves; if you want to limit the exploitation of a long-lasting effect to a specific person, you make a Key that narrows the field as closely to that person and that person alone as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>A key can be an item carried (which is a criterion), are you saying that you'd need to limit the exploitation of a long-lasting effect to that item, you make the key that narrows the field as closely to that item and that item alone as possible? And cant just use that item?<br /> <br /> Are you really saying a specific person cant qualify as a criterion for a spell because you have to symbolize them somehow? If a person isnt a symbol of themselves then what the f*ck is?<br /> <br /> Wtf has symbolism have to do with keys apart for them maybe being able to be criterion for them?<br /> <br /> You could definatly hang a key off &quot;my cabal mates that have the cabal theme merit&quot; and thats fine, that can be checked. Without it and just a normal &quot;my cabal&quot; what if somebody was kicked from a cabal, or only one person in that cabal decided a person shouldnt be in the cabal, who decides whats a member of that cabal or not? The spell sure as sh*t wouldnt know...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:19:11-07:00","id":1089507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089478#post1089478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A key can be an item carried (which is a criterion), are you saying that you'd need to limit the exploitation of a long-lasting effect to that item, you make the key that narrows the field as closely to that item and that item alone as possible? And cant just use that item?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can make a Key in practice be an item that there's only one of at the time of setting the criterion, but you can't make a one-criterion Key that will only work for one subject <i>ever</i>. &quot;An emblem of the Fire-Marked Apothecary&quot; is a valid Key; &quot;<i>Just this</i> emblem of the Fire-Marked Apothecary&quot; is going to need extra Potency to accomplish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you really saying a specific person cant qualify as a criterion for a spell because you have to symbolize them somehow? </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's how magic operates. It's a personal practice, but it's very much not a person-oriented force. This is the stuff of names and signs and signifiers, not plain humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a person isnt a symbol of themselves then what the f*ck is? </div> </div> </div>A person is a person. The things that tell you who and what that person is are where symbols live. You don't describe Bob to strangers by his Bobness unless you're just looking to infuriate them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wtf has symbolism have to do with keys apart for them maybe being able to be criterion for them? </div> </div> </div>Keys are a thing that has to do with magic and magic is a thing that runs on symbolism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could definatly hang a key off &quot;my cabal mates that have the cabal theme merit&quot; and thats fine, that can be checked. Without it and just a normal &quot;my cabal&quot; what if somebody was kicked from a cabal, or only one person in that cabal decided a person shouldnt be in the cabal, who decides whats a member of that cabal or not? The spell sure as sh*t wouldnt know... </div> </div> </div>The spell doesn't have to &quot;know.&quot; The spell just has to respond to criteria that are fairly concrete, which tend to be the sorts of things that make up cabal symbolism.<br /> <br /> One also doesn't look to restrict someone as prying as a mage from a resource without doing the simple due diligence of changing the magical locks, so &quot;what if the membership changes&quot; doesn't have much weight even if I <i>was</i> arguing that &quot;members of my cabal&quot; was a valid criterion on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:45:17-07:00","id":1089517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can make a Key in practice be an item that there's only one of at the time of setting the criterion, but you can't make a one-criterion Key that will only work for one subject <i>ever</i>. &quot;An emblem of the Fire-Marked Apothecary&quot; is a valid Key; &quot;<i>Just this</i> emblem of the Fire-Marked Apothecary&quot; is going to need extra Potency to accomplish. </div> </div> </div>Both are just one criterion, keys &amp; potency only mention number of criteria/requirements, it does not mention having to limit scope via potency, the scope can be as wide as you like. Where does it say that scope has anything to do with potency, it only mentions number of criteria/requirements. All of something or only something, are both 1 criteria with vastly different scope. You could set a key for the 21st June, and the spell would activate every 21st of June, or you could set it for 21th June 2017 and it'd only activate ont that day. The example says &quot;only open on the summer solstice&quot; theres no reason you couldnt limit it further by also stating the year 21st June 2017 is 1 criteria, 2 criteria would be 21st june 2017 at 1pm&quot;..<br /> <br /> I think you have drank to much symbolism cool aid if you think a person isnt a symbol of themselves. Magical or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Symbolism is the practice or art of using an object or a word to represent an abstract idea. An action, <u><i><b>person</b></i></u>, place, word, or object can all have a symbolic meaning. </div> </div> </div>Bob could be a shining symbol of hope,he could also have a symbolic meaning of being Bob, he's still a symbol and that symbol could be a criteria/requirement for a key. Key = &quot;that Bob the symbol of hope/bob the symbol of bob&quot;, not that other &quot;Bob who is a different symbol of hope/symbol of this bob&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:19:34-07:00","id":1089547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089517#post1089517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are just one criterion, keys &amp; potency only mention number of criteria/requirements, it does not mention having to limit scope via potency, the scope can be as wide as you like. Where does it say that scope has anything to do with potency, it only mentions number of criteria/requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>git, I realize that I am not always one-hundred percent clear with my meanings, but if you genuinely cannot understand how the scope of a Key with three criteria is more limited than the scope of a Key with one criterion then I don't feel I'm going to be making much headway in this conversation regardless of how I word my statements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you have drank to much symbolism cool aid if you think a person isnt a symbol of themselves. Magical or not. </div> </div> </div>Unwarranted intimations aside, there is no &quot;or not&quot; in this discussion. <i>We're talking about magic, specifically in the context of the Supernal powers of Awakened mages in the general setting of the Chronicles of Darkness.</i><br /> <br /> Characters becoming actual Significant Capital Letter <i>Symbols</i> of concepts exists in the game \u2014 as the product of <i>Ascension </i>to identify their likenesses with aspects of the Arcana to the point of potentially becoming Yantras for other mages. Meanwhile, nothing about the way magic works requires that a person be a symbol of themselves to function \u2014 spells are cast either at a target within the reach of one's senses or through a sympathetic connection with the aid of a representative proxy, both of which fit perfectly fine with the magical-structural equivalent of a to-whom-it-may-concern.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say nothing of how people aren't abstract ideas and a tautology is still not a meaningful description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bob could be a shining symbol of hope,he could also have a symbolic meaning of being Bob, he's still a symbol and that symbol could be a criteria/requirement for a key. Key = &quot;that Bob the symbol of hope/bob the symbol of bob&quot;, not that other &quot;Bob who is a different symbol of hope/symbol of this bob&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Bob being Bob is not a descriptive quality. In Supernal terms, Bob is a collection of qualities that are shared with many other things that could conceivably trip the Key, some of which may also be common signifiers of a thing that inspires hope if that happens to be what you're using to allow Bob privileged access to the spell's effects or loopholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:58:03-07:00","id":1089563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089547#post1089547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">git, I realize that I am not always one-hundred percent clear with my meanings, but if you genuinely cannot understand how the scope of a Key with three criteria is more limited than the scope of a Key with one criterion then I don't feel I'm going to be making much headway in this conversation regardless of how I word my statements.<br /> <br /> Unwarranted intimations aside, there is no &quot;or not&quot; in this discussion. <i>We're talking about magic, specifically in the context of the Supernal powers of Awakened mages in the general setting of the Chronicles of Darkness.</i><br /> <br /> Characters becoming actual Significant Capital Letter <i>Symbols</i> of concepts exists in the game \u2014 as the product of <i>Ascension </i>to identify their likenesses with aspects of the Arcana to the point of potentially becoming Yantras for other mages. Meanwhile, nothing about the way magic works requires that a person be a symbol of themselves to function \u2014 spells are cast either at a target within the reach of one's senses or through a sympathetic connection with the aid of a representative proxy, both of which fit perfectly fine with the magical-structural equivalent of a to-whom-it-may-concern.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say nothing of how people aren't abstract ideas and a tautology is still not a meaningful description.<br /> <br /> Bob being Bob is not a descriptive quality. In Supernal terms, Bob is a collection of qualities that are shared with many other things that could conceivably trip the Key, some of which may also be common signifiers of a thing that inspires hope if that happens to be what you're using to allow Bob privileged access to the spell's effects or loopholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, i think my example proves i already know that multiple keys can make the scope more limited, i was saying that one key can be as big a scope as you like. Hell you could key &quot;Women&quot; and have 51% of the population who can use that key. But similarly you could key it to &quot;My sister Shiela&quot; and thats still only 1 criteria but limited in scope to your sister Shiela, not your sister Barbara. Both have 1 criteria with different scopes. One key can be both very broad or very specific, it all depends.<br /> <br /> So all Bobs can trip a Key that has the criteria of one specific Bob? Ok then, whatever i hope you realise how stupid that is sometime.<br /> <br /> Say you know two Bobs, Bob Billman &amp; Bob Way, if i said &quot;Dont let Bob through your door, he'll kill you&quot; you would be well within your rights to think &quot;what Bob?&quot; because its not descriptive enough, however if both Bobs were together and i pointed at Bob Billman and said &quot;Dont let that Bob through your door, he'll kill you&quot; then thats a pretty good indication of what Bob i mean right? Same with Keys.<br /> <br /> Saying the keyed spell can determine Male from Female but cant determine Bob Billman from Bob Way is a stretch to far...oh wait i know the answer is going to be something something male/famale symbolism....blah blah...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T21:30:16-07:00","id":1089570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089547#post1089547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">git, I realize that I am not always one-hundred percent clear with my meanings, but if you genuinely cannot understand how the scope of a Key with three criteria is more limited than the scope of a Key with one criterion then I don't feel I'm going to be making much headway in this conversation regardless of how I word my statements.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Key with three criteria CAN be more broad than a key with one criterion. One key says that only people with hair, eyes, red blood can access a portal. Another key says that only people with seven fingers can access a portal. Which key is more broad and which is more narrow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T21:30:28-07:00","id":1089571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089563#post1089563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying the keyed spell can determine Male from Female but cant determine Bob Billman from Bob Way is a stretch to far...oh wait i know the answer is going to be something something male/famale symbolism....blah blah...</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bIf you are going to be rude please discontinue participating in this conversation.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T21:33:31-07:00","id":1089573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089563#post1089563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, i think my example proves i already know that multiple keys can make the scope more limited, i was saying that one key can be as big a scope as you like. Hell you could key &quot;Women&quot; and have 51% of the population who can use that key. But similarly you could key it to &quot;My sister Shiela&quot; and thats still only 1 criteria but limited in scope to your sister Shiela, not your sister Barbara. Both have 1 criteria with different scopes. One key can be both very broad or very specific, it all depends.<br /> <br /> So all Bobs can trip a Key that has the criteria of one specific Bob? Ok then, whatever i hope you realise how stupid that is sometime.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point in this argument has been consistently based on the entire supposition of One Specific Bob <i>not being a valid singular criterion</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Say you know two Bobs, Bob Billman &amp; Bob Way, if i said &quot;Dont let Bob through your door, he'll kill you&quot; you would be well within your rights to think &quot;what Bob?&quot; because its not descriptive enough, however if both Bobs were together and i pointed at Bob Billman and said &quot;Dont let that Bob through your door, he'll kill you&quot; then thats a pretty good indication of what Bob i mean right? Same with Keys. </div> </div> </div>Keys do not operate on the logic of you pointing at a dude and saying &quot;that one.&quot; Presumably Mister Billman is not indistinguishable from Mister Way in all fashions just because they share a forename. Is Billman trained as a carpenter? Is he missing a specific finger? Does he wear glasses instead of contacts? Does he live on a particular piece of property? Does his daily routine keep him at a place away from the door you don't want him getting through? These are all things that can allow you to keep Billman out of your spells with increasing degrees of certainty if you don't want to simply set up a general ward that you can key with invitations, but none of these qualities stop at &quot;is/is not Bob Billman.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saying the keyed spell can determine Male from Female but cant determine Bob Billman from Bob Way is a stretch to far...oh wait i know the answer is going to be something something male/famale symbolism....blah blah... </div> </div> </div>The spell can certainly distinguish Bob Billman from Bob Way. It just can't do that purely by the fact of those two Bobs being different people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-08-2017, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T21:50:53-07:00","id":1089576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089570#post1089570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Key with three criteria CAN be more broad than a key with one criterion. One key says that only people with hair, eyes, red blood can access a portal. Another key says that only people with seven fingers can access a portal. Which key is more broad and which is more narrow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you genuinely believe that I was talking about this type of example in the quoted section?<br /> <br /> The section where I am addressing a response to an example I gave of how one would have to add extra qualifiers to a Key to make using a unique criterion without possessing the original specimen a more involved process than simple forgery?<br /> <br /> Having seven fingers is a reproducible quality. You can be someone other than the intended user and still take advantage of the Key.<br /> <br /> Carrying a particular symbol is a reproducible quality. You can be someone other than the intended user and still take advantage of the Key.<br /> <br /> Carrying a particular symbol requires additional criteria or greater specificity to further limit access to the effect the Key seals off, but the Key will still ultimately be a reproducible quality without necessitating the use of magic to trick the spell into registering qualities that are not there, because <i>that is the narrative purpose of Keys</i>. If you don't want anyone to use a spell without your permission, you just <i>don't incorporate a key into the spell</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:06:55-07:00","id":1089578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089573#post1089573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point in this argument has been consistently based on the entire supposition of One Specific Bob <i>not being a valid singular criterion</i>.<br /> <br /> Keys do not operate on the logic of you pointing at a dude and saying &quot;that one.&quot; Presumably Mister Billman is not indistinguishable from Mister Way in all fashions just because they share a forename. Is Billman trained as a carpenter? Is he missing a specific finger? Does he wear glasses instead of contacts? Does he live on a particular piece of property? Does his daily routine keep him at a place away from the door you don't want him getting through? These are all things that can allow you to keep Billman out of your spells with increasing degrees of certainty if you don't want to simply set up a general ward that you can key with invitations, but none of these qualities stop at &quot;is/is not Bob Billman.&quot;<br /> <br /> The spell can certainly distinguish Bob Billman from Bob Way. It just can't do that purely by the fact of those two Bobs being different people.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will just have to agree to disagree. You can agree that a keyed spell can distinguish one Bob from another but cant agree why and that one would need some convoluted criteria to make sure its keyed to one and not the other when its perfectly able to have it keyed to one item and not another and that somehow people are just different because symbolism. How do you explain keying it one particular item carried and another exactly the same item also carried but not that particular one, how does symbology explain that away for items and not for people. Items can be symbols of themselves then but people cant because they are people? Makes no sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:11:59-07:00","id":1089580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089576#post1089576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you genuinely believe that I was talking about this type of example in the quoted section?<br /> <br /> The section where I am addressing a response to an example I gave of how one would have to add extra qualifiers to a Key to make using a unique criterion without possessing the original specimen a more involved process than simple forgery?<br /> <br /> Having seven fingers is a reproducible quality. You can be someone other than the intended user and still take advantage of the Key.<br /> <br /> Carrying a particular symbol is a reproducible quality. You can be someone other than the intended user and still take advantage of the Key.<br /> <br /> Carrying a particular symbol requires additional criteria or greater specificity to further limit access to the effect the Key seals off, but the Key will still ultimately be a reproducible quality without necessitating the use of magic to trick the spell into registering qualities that are not there, because <i>that is the narrative purpose of Keys</i>. If you don't want anyone to use a spell without your permission, you just <i>don't incorporate a key into the spell</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that Bob who was there when you cast the colocate spell for the portal is a reproducible quality. You either are that Bob or arn't that Bob and a key is born. If i want my colocated portal to only be usable by certain people i really do need to key it otherwise anyone who can see it can use it....not keying it isnt going to stop them being able to use it without my permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:19:56-07:00","id":1089583,"title":"","content":"*Considers* The thing is, I think that while you can technically key a window so that no one can open the window except a certain person, that doesn't actually stop people from looking through the window - and if you key it to be one way, the person your adding a key for would, in fact, only be able to see through the window from the way that you can see it through. If you set it that it can be viewed both ways then while, yes, a key might be possible to add - the window would in fact be visible to anyone around that person - not just the person who opened it up. Fate on the other hand can make it so that it is viewable (not 'open' or 'closed') one way, <i>except in regards to &quot;this&quot;</i>. (&quot;This&quot; being whatever you exempt - because selective exemption is a fate thing.)<br /> <br /> Of course none of this stops a mage with space from seeing there is a window in space there to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:32:44-07:00","id":1089586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089578#post1089578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We will just have to agree to disagree. You can agree that a keyed spell can distinguish one Bob from another but cant agree why and that one would need some convoluted criteria to make sure its keyed to one and not the other when its perfectly able to have it keyed to one item and not another and that somehow people are just different because symbolism. How do you explain keying it one particular item carried and another exactly the same item also carried but not that particular one, how does symbology explain that away for items and not for people. Items can be symbols of themselves then but people cant because they are people? Makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It &quot;makes no sense&quot; because you're not listening to what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> &quot;A particular symbol&quot; is not &quot;the signet ring owned by Vicar Denarius as a token of his membership in the Green Orbit cabal, and no other such ring,&quot; it's &quot;any ring made of the same material and/or bearing the same design as the signet ring of Vicar Denarius (who has that ring because etc).&quot; You can make another ring like that to trip the Key if you don't have the resources to steal and retain the Vicar's signet ring.<br /> <br /> This isn't &quot;people and items are different,&quot; this is &quot;particular specimens (be they people or items or animals or what have you) aren't criteria unto themselves even if you'd have to work to make them not the only specimens of their criteria.&quot;<br /> <br /> This does, in fact, mean that mages who want to strictly limit who can bypass their spells tend to make use of criteria that are too convoluted to luck into and still pretty tricky to bring together on purpose. That's how wizards do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089580#post1089580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being that Bob who was there when you cast the colocate spell for the portal is a reproducible quality. You either are that Bob or arn't that Bob and a key is born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you understand what &quot;reproducible&quot; means?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If i want my colocated portal to only be usable by certain people i really do need to key it otherwise anyone who can see it can use it....not keying it isnt going to stop them being able to use it without my permission. </div> </div> </div>And you can manage that without having to set a Key based on criteria that mean absolutely nothing without a larger context. Give them a password or a token or a membership to a defined group or literally anything else that could conceivably be stumbled upon or worked around. Give them a passcode that isn't just &quot;It's me, you know, the guy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:12:19-07:00","id":1089600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089576#post1089576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carrying a particular symbol requires additional criteria or greater specificity to further limit access to the effect the Key seals off, but the Key will still ultimately be a reproducible quality without necessitating the use of magic to trick the spell into registering qualities that are not there, because <i>that is the narrative purpose of Keys</i>. If you don't want anyone to use a spell without your permission, you just <i>don't incorporate a key into the spell</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then if that was meant to be the narrative purpose of keys, then the developers utterly failed to communicate it within the text, as nothing in it says that a key must be reproducible. Moreover, if I as the storyteller can't establish a coherent in-world reason why specific people can't be keys, it becomes unfair to the players to deny it arbitrarily. A big part of the fun of the game is encouraging players to use the creative thaumaturgy system, and that system doesn't work when you tie the players down with a bunch of obscure fiddly minutae for them to constantly keep track of. That's the whole reason why the devs reworked the spell list for 2nd edition to follow the practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089586#post1089586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you understand what &quot;reproducible&quot; means?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of mages, he's technically right. If your name is Bob, you could go back in time to when the spell was cast, so that you also satisfy the condition, allowing you to reproduce the key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-08-2017, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:15:51-07:00","id":1089602,"title":"","content":"Double-post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:55:37-07:00","id":1089616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089600#post1089600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then if that was meant to be the narrative purpose of keys, then the developers utterly failed to communicate it within the text, as nothing in it says that a key must be reproducible.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about a genre emulation tool that is used to allow Awakened magic to produce restrictions that exist in other gamelines under the same generic name \u2014 Shadow Verges, Hedge Gates, and Avernian Gates have all had special criteria that allowed mortals to open them that were called &quot;keys,&quot; and the Mage 2e spellcasting concept occupies the same niche.<br /> <br /> Characters (and other phenomena) have supernatural qualities for reasons that go beyond &quot;because they're them&quot; because that allows things to be said about those characters through their relation with those qualities and the circumstances that underlie them. This goes unstated because it usually doesn't need to be said if you're trying to make a game where the characters and the setting actually fit together (or at least make an interface with each other).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, if I as the storyteller can't establish a coherent in-world reason why specific people can't be keys, it becomes unfair to the players to deny it arbitrarily. </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you wouldn't ever use it as a requirement for a naturally-occurring supernatural effect, you shouldn't allow it on player-created Keys&quot; is triflingly easy to back-justify into in-setting lore. &quot;Balthazar can open this door because he's Balthazar&quot; with no further elaboration is an incoherent tautology in a way that &quot;Balthazar can open this door because he knows and says the password&quot; or &quot;Balthazar can open this door because he was present for its creation&quot; are not.<br /> <br /> It's not arbitrary to veto the use of readings of the rules that make a game of Mage fail to work like a game about mages. The world runs over with weird secrets that are personal in scope but impersonal in medium and this world shapes mages in such a manner that they emulate their findings where applicable instead of immediately jumping to technical readings of a rulebook that does not exist as a comprehensive and infallible in-universe artifact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A big part of the fun of the game is encouraging players to use the creative thaumaturgy system, and that system doesn't work when you tie the players down with a bunch of obscure fiddly minutae for them to constantly keep track of. That's the whole reason why the devs reworked the spell list for 2nd edition to follow the practices. </div> </div> </div>And a big part of my issue with the fanbase stems from people assuming that they don't need to rein in their imagination and then complaining when the system is built for a more constrained setting but didn't have the wordcount to devote to delineating the full extent of what you can't specifically accomplish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the context of mages, he's technically right. </div> </div> </div>Nope. No amount of time travel is going to make you &quot;that Bob&quot; without locking the Bob he's talking about out of the selfsame effect. That is the nature of the disagreement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-08-2017, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T00:33:03-07:00","id":1089625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089616#post1089616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about a genre emulation tool that is used to allow Awakened magic to produce restrictions that exist in other gamelines under the same generic name \u2014 Shadow Verges, Hedge Gates, and Avernian Gates have all had special criteria that allowed mortals to open them that were called &quot;keys,&quot; and the Mage 2e spellcasting concept occupies the same niche.<br /> <br /> Characters (and other phenomena) have supernatural qualities for reasons that go beyond &quot;because they're them&quot; because that allows things to be said about those characters through their relation with those qualities and the circumstances that underlie them. This goes unstated because it usually doesn't need to be said if you're trying to make a game where the characters and the setting actually fit together (or at least make an interface with each other).<br /> <br /> &quot;If you wouldn't ever use it as a requirement for a naturally-occurring supernatural effect, you shouldn't allow it on player-created Keys&quot; is triflingly easy to back-justify into in-setting lore. If you can't conceive of why &quot;Balthazar can open this door because he's Balthazar&quot; with no further elaboration is an incoherent tautology in a way that &quot;Balthazar can open this door because he knows and says the password&quot; or &quot;Balthazar can open this door because he was present for its creation&quot; are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally understand why those make for more interesting stories, but I still don't see why supernal magic must be bound by the same restrictions as any other phenomena. Fate Oaths work nothing like a Changeling's magic, for example. A Mage can simply choose to end their oath whenever they please just by cancelling the spell, whereas a Changeling's oaths, once set, are enforced by the Wyrd itself. I think that Fate would be more interesting if a Mage could choose to bind themselves into meaningful oaths, but I'm not going to redesign Fate because of it.<br /> <br /> Supernal magic works on Imagos. If a player can clearly and explicitly define the parameters of their spell, it's unfair of me to say they can't cast it, just because I think it would be more interesting if there were some other restriction that's not in the book. Balthazar can open this door because that is how the spell was imagined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not arbitrary to veto the use of readings of the rules that make a game of Mage fail to work like a game about mages. The world runs over with weird secrets that are personal in scope but impersonal in medium and this world shapes mages in such a manner that they emulate their findings where applicable instead of immediately jumping to technical readings of a rulebook that does not exist as a comprehensive and infallible in-universe artifact. </div> </div> </div>Mages may not think in terms of rules, but players must think in those terms. If a designer cannot precisely define exactly what they mean in the rules, it ruins the creative thaumaturgy system for the players. If I'm trying to encourage the players to be creative and think of cool new spells, and then I have to turn around at every other suggestion and say &quot;no, you can't do that because this stipulation that's not in the book, which I never told you about before&quot;, I am violating their agency as players. More than that, I'm ruining the sense of creative freedom that makes the magic system special.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a big part of my issue with the fanbase stems from people assuming that they don't need to rein in their imagination and then complaining when the system is built for a more constrained setting but didn't have the wordcount to devote to delineating the full extent of what you can't specifically accomplish. </div> </div> </div>It's hard enough to learn how the magic system works without unstated rules throwing you for a loop. If the developers couldn't explicitly state something important in the rules, then they failed in their goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 05-08-2017, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:33:37-07:00","id":1089639,"title":"","content":"Probably not too helpful to this conversation, but I can't help but feel like defining a 'person' with space - literally defining just them - seems like it would be a complex thing to do. I mean, mages opt to change who they are all the time. Every day of their life in fact, through the use of Shadow Names. Because of this, if a Mage who was named Bob but went by the Shadow Name Balthazar was a valid 'option' to pick - and was Balthazar when the portal declared him to be 'the key' - I can't help but feel like Bob could not get in - unless he was in fact within his &quot;Balthazar&quot; Persona. Just a random musing.<br /> <br /> ... On a separate train of thought:<br /> <br /> I think - and this is my own personal opinion - that it is entirely possible to key a person to a gate or portal or a what-have-you. What isn't possible, however, is keying -two- specific, different people and expecting the lock to unlike for either one of them. For instance, making a gate which only I can open is fine. Making a gate which only I and my cabal mate (we'll call them Azure) can open is a bit more difficult - because if you -include- Azure than you would need both myself -and- Azure to open the lock. I could not get the spell to selectively accept either one of us - in the same way that I can make a key more complex and difficult to get into, but I could not make a key and then make an 'alternative' key. This is my personal reason why people go so far as to specify things like 'bloodlines' or 'a password', because while I can't be Azure and myself at the same time, I -can- have my cabal's personal tattoo on my shoulder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T02:48:52-07:00","id":1089669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Key</b> \u2014 a particular item carried,<br /> password spoken, or other criterion that either <u>activates</u> a spell<br /> or <u>bypasses</u> its effects.<b>The Key may have a number of requirements<br /> equal to the spell\u2019s Potency.</b> </div> </div> </div>Spell can either activate or bypass the effect of the spell for a single person(&quot;visible to anyone of the mage\u2019s bloodline&quot;) or for everyone(&quot;open on the summer solstice&quot;). 'Visible to anyone with Bob Somebody sympathetic name' is as much possible check for a spell as 'mages bloodline'. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Single Key should be dependent of its complexity, sure, but you could take this Reach multiple times, I think, and specify Reach x Keys .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:02:39-07:00","id":1089712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089586#post1089586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It &quot;makes no sense&quot; because you're not listening to what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> &quot;A particular symbol&quot; is not &quot;the signet ring owned by Vicar Denarius as a token of his membership in the Green Orbit cabal, and no other such ring,&quot; it's &quot;any ring made of the same material and/or bearing the same design as the signet ring of Vicar Denarius (who has that ring because etc).&quot; You can make another ring like that to trip the Key if you don't have the resources to steal and retain the Vicar's signet ring.<br /> <br /> This isn't &quot;people and items are different,&quot; this is &quot;particular specimens (be they people or items or animals or what have you) aren't criteria unto themselves even if you'd have to work to make them not the only specimens of their criteria.&quot;<br /> <br /> This does, in fact, mean that mages who want to strictly limit who can bypass their spells tend to make use of criteria that are too convoluted to luck into and still pretty tricky to bring together on purpose. That's how wizards do.<br /> <br /> Do you understand what &quot;reproducible&quot; means?<br /> <br /> And you can manage that without having to set a Key based on criteria that mean absolutely nothing without a larger context. Give them a password or a token or a membership to a defined group or literally anything else that could conceivably be stumbled upon or worked around. Give them a passcode that isn't just &quot;It's me, you know, the guy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Text says &quot;a particular <b>item</b> carried&quot; not particular symbol carried which surely can be Vicar Denarius' ring and not any other ring. If i define it as &quot;the teddy bear i gave my son Bob&quot; (then as your casting the spell your imagining &quot;that&quot; bear into the imago and the key will later be able to go &quot;is this that bear yes/no&quot;. You seem to imagine that somebody can trick the key by going to some shop, buying the exact same bear and voila you have the same key even though its not the bear i gave my son Bob.<br /> <br /> We have both written huge passages on something thats one paragraph in the book, and im not sure where you get all these ideas from but if you like having your players jump through hoops then thats fine but unless you have read more than the paragraph in the core book on the subject anything your writing about is your own interpretation and so far the only view on that side of the argument.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-08-2017, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T05:17:30-07:00","id":1089716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089639#post1089639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not too helpful to this conversation, but I can't help but feel like defining a 'person' with space - literally defining just them - seems like it would be a complex thing to do. I mean, mages opt to change who they are all the time. Every day of their life in fact, through the use of Shadow Names. Because of this, if a Mage who was named Bob but went by the Shadow Name Balthazar was a valid 'option' to pick - and was Balthazar when the portal declared him to be 'the key' - I can't help but feel like Bob could not get in - unless he was in fact within his &quot;Balthazar&quot; Persona. Just a random musing.<br /> <br /> ... On a separate train of thought:<br /> <br /> I think - and this is my own personal opinion - that it is entirely possible to key a person to a gate or portal or a what-have-you. What isn't possible, however, is keying -two- specific, different people and expecting the lock to unlike for either one of them. For instance, making a gate which only I can open is fine. Making a gate which only I and my cabal mate (we'll call them Azure) can open is a bit more difficult - because if you -include- Azure than you would need both myself -and- Azure to open the lock. I could not get the spell to selectively accept either one of us - in the same way that I can make a key more complex and difficult to get into, but I could not make a key and then make an 'alternative' key. This is my personal reason why people go so far as to specify things like 'bloodlines' or 'a password', because while I can't be Azure and myself at the same time, I -can- have my cabal's personal tattoo on my shoulder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fine, if a key is &quot;The mage Balthazar&quot; and Bob has some merit or whatever than makes the difference between Bob and Balthazar distinct enough then yes, Bob in his mundane guise wouldnt open that key. I see no problem with this.<br /> <br /> If you key a password and dont tell anybody only you know it, but if you need somebody else to be able to bypass/activate your spell you can also give them the key. If it were possible to key to &quot;all cabal&quot; members (which i think it might be if you have the cabal merits) its a far harder task to define who is and isnt a member of your cabal. If they key is &quot;all members of the Banana cabal&quot; then being a member of the Banana cabal has to be backed up with something non subjective like having the cabal merit (so technically you could be in the cabal not have the merit but you wouldnt count as a key). Even this is getting into whiffy territory tho..<br /> <br /> Intresting question tho, if you add a key, does the first key have to be yourself or are you always able to use your own spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-08-2017, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat