e Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:55:31-07:00","id":1089981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089669#post1089669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Single Key should be dependent of its complexity, sure, but you could take this Reach multiple times, I think, and specify Reach x Keys .</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you could - taking the reach multiple times wouldn't change the fact that you would need both components. That's what I'm saying. If you have a door that is locked twice, using two different keys, you don't get through the door with only one key. It's the same logic that I'm following here. You might have multiple copies of that key (like members of a bloodline), but having two distinctly different keys that both work on the same lock is not possible - each key would work on it's own lock, and all the locks would need to be unlocked to open the door.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:06:47-07:00","id":1089987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089981#post1089981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if you could - taking the reach multiple times wouldn't change the fact that you would need both components. That's what I'm saying. If you have a door that is locked twice, using two different keys, you don't get through the door with only one key. It's the same logic that I'm following here. You might have multiple copies of that key (like members of a bloodline), but having two distinctly different keys that both work on the same lock is not possible - each key would work on it's own lock, and all the locks would need to be unlocked to open the door.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a valid and coherent assumption. It doesn't apeal to me since Reach is for expanding and refining a spell and in this case having more options of opening a door, Door, Doors can aid it. If player can spend Reach to achieve it I would allow it. +5 Reach for five members of the cabal as Keys of already Reach heavy Co-location spell for example. But you know, I'm me. And as I said your interpretation is coherent and I approve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:27:49-07:00","id":1089999,"title":"","content":"I personally think that each reach option provides the spell with another method of activating/bypassing that spell that is separate from each other but individually will work.<br /> <br /> Sudocode maybe?<br /> <br /> If has key 1 (member of bloodline) return open portal, <i>(or has key 2 (peeble) return open portal)</i><br /> else if has key 2 (pebble) return open portal<br /> else return keep portal closed.<br /> <br /> My coding is terrible but i think its logically possible for there to be multiple different keys all able to activate/bypass a spell and one could prove it via code <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (OR statements?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:47:45-07:00","id":1090008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089999#post1089999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that each reach option provides the spell with another method of activating/bypassing that spell that is separate from each other but individually will work.<br /> <br /> Sudocode maybe?<br /> <br /> If has key 1 (member of bloodline) return open portal, <i>(or has key 2 (peeble) return open portal)</i><br /> else if has key 2 (pebble) return open portal<br /> else return keep portal closed.<br /> <br /> My coding is terrible but i think its logically possible for there to be multiple different keys all able to activate/bypass a spell and one could prove it via code <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (OR statements?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Pseudocode is fine tbh. My issue with that line of thought tends to be that 'conditional circumstances' tends to be more the providence of Fate than Space. A key is a key - it locks or unlocks something. It's a password, a biometric scanner, a token card you insert in order to open a door. Fate is the one that sets up the program to say '&quot;If this occurs, then this must happen&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T19:48:43-07:00","id":1090096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089783#post1089783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And he's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be possible to get a more detailed explanation for why mages with the ability to set Keys would ever bother with more complex Keys than &quot;anyone we want in&quot; for spells that aren't part of a specifically esoteric line of inquiry like having access to a given building filtered down to members of a given company?<br /> <br /> I ask because the even-marginally-more-esoteric Keys like saying a password or showing up at a certain time seem more likely to foster odd behaviors among mages and Sleepwalkers that provide story hooks than do Keys that to a casual Awakened interloper in practice translate to &quot;brute-force it with Veiling or Dispellation&quot; due to the ease with which the latter becomes a wall that can only be surmounted by a very broad and basic plot thread of &quot;get stronger to crack open this secret door that only opens for its maker&quot; instead of &quot;investigate the Mystery of this cult that wears coats with blue liners and has a High Speech rune of lightning burned into the side of their getaway car that just vanished into this blind alley&quot; or what have you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T01:02:27-07:00","id":1090166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1088689-can-others-see-your-scrying-window?p=1089793#post1089793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you ever considered a Patreon where we could pay you for answering questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a breach of my contract.<br /> <br /> No one who's written for a gameline is allowed to take money for providing resources usable with that gameline except when properly licensed through White Wolf / Onyx Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"use